/target
/build

# Arch packaging: `makepkg` in `packaging/arch` writes its work tree (`src/`,
# `pkg/`), the tag tarball it downloads and the packages it builds beside the
# PKGBUILD, because it defaults `BUILDDIR`, `SRCDEST` and `PKGDEST` to the
# directory the PKGBUILD is in (`makepkg`'s own `canonicalize_path` loop).
/packaging/arch/src/
/packaging/arch/pkg/
/packaging/arch/*.tar.gz
/packaging/arch/*.pkg.tar.*
